# Engine and tools

`core/engine` is the shared kernel: sample, clip, bake, composite, export. Method names are those steps. Keep bodies linear. The engine does not know which tool is selected.

`core/tools` is one class per tool that implements `DrawingTool`. Pencil is first. Add other tool files only when that tool is built (brush, crayon, marker, watercolor, spray paint, glitter, pattern, paint bucket, sticker). No empty stubs. No `extensions/` or `logging/` folders.

A new tool is a new class. Do not add `switch (brushType)` in the engine, screen, or ViewModel. `core/engine` never imports a concrete tool.

```dart
// BAD
void paint(Canvas canvas, BrushType type) {
  switch (type) {
    case BrushType.pencil: _drawPencil(canvas);
    case BrushType.marker: _drawMarker(canvas);
  }
}

// GOOD
abstract class DrawingTool {
  void paint(Canvas canvas);
}
class PencilTool implements DrawingTool {
  void paint(Canvas canvas) { /* dabs via the engine */ }
}
```
